    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "name": "Foot of the Lighthouse",
      "description": "The lighthouse is taller than it looked from below, and whiter too, streaked with salt. The door hangs open on one hinge. Inside, an iron stair goes up in a spiral into the dark. The cliff path goes back south.",
      "connections": { "north": 4, "south": 2 },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "foot-climb",
          "triggers": ["climb*", "up", "go up", "*stair*", "ascend*", "enter*", "go in*", "*door*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "changelocation", "parameters": ["4"] }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "name": "The Lamp Room",
      "description": "At the top of the stair is a round room made of glass. The great lamp sits in the middle, a brass reservoir under a crown of lenses, and it is cold and dark. The glass all around you looks out on nothing but grey sea and sky. A small wooden box is screwed to the wall beside the stair. The stair goes back down (south).",
      "connections": { "south": 3 },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-down",
          "triggers": ["down", "go down", "descend*", "climb down*", "*stair*", "leave*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "changelocation", "parameters": ["3"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-fill",
          "triggers": ["*pour*", "*fill*", "*oil*", "*reservoir*"],
          "if": ["carrying:lamp oil"],
          "ifNot": ["lamp_filled"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "removeitems", "parameters": ["lamp oil"] },
            { "action": "addcondition", "parameters": ["lamp_filled"], "scope": "world" },
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["You pull the stopper and pour. The oil runs thick and slow into the brass reservoir, and the wick soaks it up and darkens. The room smells of it now. The lamp is ready. It only needs a flame."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-light",
          "triggers": ["*light*", "*strike*", "*flint*", "*ignite*", "*kindle*", "*fire*", "*spark*", "*flame*"],
          "if": ["lamp_filled", "carrying:flint and steel"],
          "ifNot": ["lamp_lit"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "addcondition", "parameters": ["lamp_lit"], "scope": "world" },
            { "action": "setlocationdescription", "parameters": ["4", "At the top of the stair is a round room made of glass. The great lamp is burning in the middle of it, and the lenses around it catch the flame and turn slowly, sending a long white beam out over the sea and back across the land. Someone lit it. The room is warm now. A small wooden box is screwed to the wall beside the stair. The stair goes back down (south)."] },
            { "action": "setlocationdescription", "parameters": ["1", "You stand on a shingle beach at the edge of evening. The sea draws back and comes in again, turning over the stones. Above you on the cliff the lighthouse is burning, and every little while its beam sweeps across the beach and lights up every wet stone at once, then moves on. North, the cliff path climbs toward the light. East are the ribs of the wreck. West, the salt marsh. South, the jetty, and out beyond it a small answering light rides on the water.\n\n(Type 'help' if you want it.)"] },
            { "action": "setlocationdescription", "parameters": ["10", "The jetty runs a long way out over the water on black, weed-hung posts, and some planks are missing. At the far end a ship's bell hangs from a crooked iron arm. Out on the water a lantern bobs, low and yellow: a boat is waiting now that the lighthouse is burning again. The beach is back north."] },
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["You strike the steel against the flint once, twice, and the third time a spark catches the wick. A small blue flame spreads, turns yellow, and then turns white as the lenses gather it up. With a groan of old clockwork the crown of glass starts to turn, and the beam goes out over the dark water.\n\nFar out, a small light answers. Then it starts coming closer.\n\nThis stays lit. Everyone who comes to this coast after you will find it burning."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-light-noflint",
          "triggers": ["*light*", "*strike*", "*flint*", "*ignite*", "*kindle*", "*fire*", "*spark*", "*flame*"],
          "if": ["lamp_filled"],
          "ifNot": ["lamp_lit"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The wick has soaked up the oil and is ready to burn, but you have nothing to light it with. There's no fire up here. The keeper must have kept a flint somewhere, probably wherever the keeper lived."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-light-dry",
          "triggers": ["*light*", "*strike*", "*flint*", "*ignite*", "*kindle*", "*fire*", "*spark*", "*flame*", "*lamp*", "*wick*"],
          "ifNot": ["lamp_filled", "lamp_lit"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The lamp's brass reservoir is empty and the wick has gone dry and stiff. Even with a flame, it would only smoulder. It needs oil first. Lamp oil comes by ship, and the only ship on this coast is the one wrecked on the beach."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-lit-look",
          "triggers": ["*lamp*", "*light*", "*lens*", "*beam*", "*wick*"],
          "if": ["lamp_lit"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The lamp is burning steadily. You didn't necessarily light it. Someone did, and it's still going. The beam goes out, comes around, goes out again, like something breathing very slowly."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-box-token",
          "triggers": ["*box*", "*token*", "open*"],
          "if": ["lamp_lit"],
          "once": true,
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The box opens easily now that the lamp is warm. The wood must have swelled in the cold. Inside is a heap of brass tokens, more than you could count, each stamped with a lighthouse. There's a card tacked inside the lid, in a careful hand:\n\n  ONE FOR EACH WHO WOULD CROSS.\n  THE FERRY COMES ONLY TO THE LIGHT.\n\nYou take one."] },
            { "action": "additems", "parameters": ["brass token"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-box-again",
          "triggers": ["*box*", "*token*", "open*"],
          "if": ["lamp_lit"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The box is still full of tokens. The card says one for each who would cross, and you already have yours. If you lost it, someone else is carrying it now."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "lamp-box-shut",
          "triggers": ["*box*", "*token*", "open*"],
          "ifNot": ["lamp_lit"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The little box is shut. The damp has swollen the lid tight into the frame, and it won't budge in this cold. Something rattles inside when you knock on it: a lot of small metal things."] }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "name": "The Wreck",
      "description": "The ship lies on its side in the sand, and the tide has been taking it apart for years. The ribs curve up black against the sky. Rope rots in heaps. A long boathook is jammed between two timbers. On the east side, a breach in the hull opens onto the hold, where water still stands black and still. The beach is west.",
      "connections": { "east": 7, "west": 1 },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "wreck-boathook",
          "triggers": ["*boathook*", "*hook*", "*pole*"],
          "once": true,
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["You work the boathook loose from the timbers. It comes free with a crack and a shower of wet splinters."] },
            { "action": "additems", "parameters": ["boathook"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "wreck-boathook-again",
          "triggers": ["*boathook*", "*hook*", "*pole*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["There's another boathook wedged deeper in the wreck. Somehow there always is. Ships carried a lot of them, and this one lost everything else."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "wreck-name",
          "triggers": ["*name*", "*ship*", "*hull*", "*bow*", "*read*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["Letters are carved into the bow, most of them worn away: -ELL KEEP-. The rest belong to the sea now."] }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "name": "The Hold",
      "description": "Inside the hull it's dim and it stinks of rot and salt. Black water stands knee-deep, and broken barrels bob in it. Nearly everything of value was carried off long ago, or sank. Grey light comes in through the breach to the west.",
      "connections": { "west": 6 },
      "monster": "conger eel",
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "hold-barrels",
          "triggers": ["*barrel*", "*cask*", "*oil*", "*flask*", "*water*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The barrels are all staved in and empty. If there was ever lamp oil aboard, the only thing down here that still has any is whatever is coiled in the deep water holding it. Or whatever was."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "hold-feed",
          "triggers": ["*feed*", "*offer*", "*give*", "*throw*", "*bread*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["You hold something out over the water. The eel's eye follows it without interest. It isn't hungry for that. It's guarding the flask, not waiting for a meal. Whatever you mean to do about it, you'll have to decide."] }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "name": "The Salt Marsh",
      "description": "The ground turns to tussock and black water, crossed by a raised causeway of old planks. Reeds hiss in the wind. Wading birds lift off at your step and settle again further away. North, where the ground rises a little, stand the tumbled walls of a cottage. The beach is east.",
      "connections": { "north": 9, "east": 1 },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "marsh-birds",
          "triggers": ["*bird*", "*reed*", "*listen*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The birds don't mind you much. When you stand still long enough the reeds go quiet, and you can hear the sea on one side and nothing at all on the other."] }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "name": "The Keeper's Cottage",
      "description": "Three walls still stand and the roof has fallen in. There's a stone hearth against the back wall with a shelf above it, and a narrow bed frame with no bed. On the shelf sits a book gone soft with damp. The marsh is back south.",
      "connections": { "south": 8 },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "cottage-hearth",
          "triggers": ["*hearth*", "*fireplace*", "*shelf*", "*flint*", "*chimney*"],
          "once": true,
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["You feel along the hearthstone, and in a dry niche under the shelf, where the keeper would reach without looking, your fingers find a flint and a steel tied together with tarred string."] },
            { "action": "additems", "parameters": ["flint and steel"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cottage-hearth-again",
          "triggers": ["*hearth*", "*fireplace*", "*shelf*", "*flint*", "*chimney*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The niche under the shelf is empty now, but only for you. Something about this place hands each visitor what they need once, and no more."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cottage-book",
          "triggers": ["*book*", "*log*", "*read*", "*journal*", "*page*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["It's the keeper's log. Most of the pages are fused together, but the last written one comes apart:\n\n  'The oil ship went down on the bar tonight. I watched it happen from the gallery. There will be no more oil, and after this the lamp will not last the winter.\n\n  I used to think I kept the light for the ships. There have not been ships in years. I think now that I keep it for whoever comes next, someone I will never see, who will look up and know somebody was here.\n\n  If you are reading this, the light has gone out. I am sorry. Please light it again. Not for me.'\n\nThe rest of the page is water-stain."] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "cottage-bed",
          "triggers": ["*bed*", "*sleep*", "*rest*", "*lie*"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["You lie on the bare slats for a while and look up through the missing roof. The sky is the colour of a bruise going yellow. It isn't comfortable, but for a little while you aren't afraid."] }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "name": "The Jetty",
      "description": "The jetty runs a long way out over the water on black, weed-hung posts, and some planks are missing. At the far end a ship's bell hangs from a crooked iron arm, green with age. Out on the water there is nothing but grey. The beach is back north.",
      "connections": { "north": 1 },
      "interactions": [
        {
          "interactionId": "jetty-bell-lit",
          "triggers": ["*bell*", "*ring*", "*signal*", "*wave*", "*call*", "*boat*", "*ferry*", "*board*", "wait*"],
          "if": ["lamp_lit"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The bell's note rolls out across the water. The lantern on the water turns toward you, and a low black ferry comes alongside the end of the jetty. It knocks gently against the posts. The ferryman doesn't speak. He holds out one open hand, palm up, and nods toward the bench."] },
            { "action": "changelocation", "parameters": ["11"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "interactionId": "jetty-bell-dark",
          "triggers": ["*bell*", "*ring*", "*signal*", "*wave*", "*call*", "*boat*", "*ferry*", "*board*", "wait*"],
          "ifNot": ["lamp_lit"],
          "actions": [
            { "action": "describe", "parameters": ["The bell's note rolls out across the water and nothing comes back. For a moment, very far out, you think you see a lantern, but in the dark it turns away. Whatever's out there won't come in to a dark coast."] }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
